WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:08.546
Hi!

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.546
I'm Ana.

00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:11.158
Welcome to 'What to Say'!

00:00:32.005 --> 00:00:36.130
Do you know what to say when you want to check your understanding?

00:00:36.294 --> 00:00:40.720
Listen out for useful language for checking your understanding.

00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:43.951
Then, we'll practise saying the new phrases –

00:00:43.994 --> 00:00:45.634
after this.

00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:48.900
This isn't right.

00:00:50.974 --> 00:00:52.911
Hey! Excuse me, Paul,

00:00:52.951 --> 00:00:54.646
could you pass me the hammer?

00:00:54.732 --> 00:00:57.349
Sorry, Bob, my ears are blocked.

00:00:57.443 --> 00:00:59.763
 I can't hear you very well.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:02.034
Could you say that again, please?

00:01:02.446 --> 00:01:03.562
The hammer.

00:01:03.633 --> 00:01:05.992
Please could you pass it to me?

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:07.586
The spanner?

00:01:07.954 --> 00:01:09.664
No. The hammer!

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:11.836
Sorry, Bob,

00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:15.498
I don't understand. This is the spanner!

00:01:15.748 --> 00:01:18.154
No, Paul, I need the hammer.

00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:21.459
It's in the toolbox, on the left, under the scissors.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:25.925
Sorry, Bob. Could you repeat that more slowly, please?

00:01:26.097 --> 00:01:27.534
The hammer …

00:01:27.816 --> 00:01:30.128
in the toolbox …

00:01:31.488 --> 00:01:32.847
on the left …

00:01:33.121 --> 00:01:34.465
under the scissors.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.637
On the left … under the scissors …

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.746
Oh! Do you mean the hammer?

00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:41.075
Is this it?

00:01:41.207 --> 00:01:42.887
Yes, that's right!

00:01:42.962 --> 00:01:46.485
Ah! Why didn't you say so?

00:01:47.494 --> 00:01:48.688
I did!

00:01:50.423 --> 00:01:51.571
Hello again!

00:01:51.665 --> 00:01:52.813
Oh dear.

00:01:52.861 --> 00:01:55.594
I think Paul needs to go home and sleep.

00:01:56.024 --> 00:02:01.617
So, did you notice the useful phrases used for checking your understanding?

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.312
 Listen to me and then repeat.

00:02:04.516 --> 00:02:05.516
I'm sorry?

00:02:07.738 --> 00:02:08.738
I'm sorry?

00:02:11.293 --> 00:02:13.206
I can't hear you very well.

00:02:16.332 --> 00:02:18.300
I can't hear you very well.

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:23.798
Could you say that again, please?

00:02:26.908 --> 00:02:29.108
Could you say that again, please?

00:02:32.539 --> 00:02:34.140
I don't understand.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.749
I don't understand.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.117
Can you repeat that more slowly, please?

00:02:48.372 --> 00:02:51.168
Can you repeat that more slowly, please?

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.340
Do you mean the hammer?

00:02:59.737 --> 00:03:01.270
Do you mean the hammer?

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.620
Is this it?

00:03:07.958 --> 00:03:08.958
Is this it?

00:03:11.396 --> 00:03:13.403
Yes, that's right!

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:17.783
Yes, that's right!

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:27.661
Try and use some of these phrases the next time you want to check your understanding in English.

00:03:27.919 --> 00:03:29.466
 Bye for now!

